# buddha: its .moddata keys (amix-dlm C3-1 section 3, C4-2 section 1 and
# section 8.2) and the definition line, as the ABI kit's mkmod reads a Master.
# One Master for both lines: no $cpu, the kit's fragment gives the line's.
# $class root: loaded by the core's root pass before the root is mounted; a
# root-class module is never unloaded ($unload never).
# $match: the Catweasel Z-II (manufacturer 0x1212, product 0x2A) and the
# stand-in mobo:buddha for the Buddha (product 0x00, every revision).  The
# 1.1 kernels' module core refuses a zorro key whose product is 00, so the
# Buddha's own key zorro:1212:00 cannot be listed yet; mobo:buddha is in the
# kit's motherboard registry with no probe, and the core passes every mobo:
# key, so the module is linked wherever its generation carries it.
# buddha_load finds the boards itself with autocon() (product 0x00 and 0x2A)
# and returns ENXIO, silently, when there is none.  When kernels whose core
# takes product 00 ship (amix-dlm core patch 0055, kabi minor 5), the line
# becomes $match zorro:1212:00,zorro:1212:2a (amix-dlm C4-2 section 8.2
# item 7).
# $rank ide: sd's class 4 (C4-1 section 4), the argument buddha_load passes
# to sd_register, once per board.  No $majors: sd owns the disk majors.
# $modtype misc: MOD_HDRV_WRAPPER, no switch-table slot.
# Parameters: intr 1 = attach INT2 after the self-test (the default), 0 =
# polled I/O; slave 1 = master and slave on every port (the default), 0 =
# masters only, 2 = a slave only if it is an ATAPI device; debug 0..2.
# The units are fixed: port 0 master 6, slave 5; port 1 3 and 2; port 2
# (Catweasel Z-II) 1 and 0.
$modtype misc
$class root
$match zorro:1212:2a,mobo:buddha
$rank ide
$unload never
$param intr:int:1:0:1
$param slave:int:1:0:2
$param debug:int:0:0:2
$desc Buddha and Catweasel Z-II IDE, root-class disk controller
buddha	buddha
